@model PrintOverview
@* Printing: a parts list that runs over several pages (its header repeats on each) and bin labels on A4 sheets. Each
   link opens a print view on a blank page, which prints itself. The Blazor sample links to the same two views. *@
<app-page-header pretitle="Tables" title="Printing" subtitle="Print views set their own page (size, orientation and margin), repeat a table's header on every page, and print labels on a sheet, one sheet per page."></app-page-header>

<div class="m-row-cards m-cols-2">
    <div class="m-card">
        <div class="m-card-body">
            <h3 class="m-card-title">Parts list</h3>
            <p class="m-muted">@Model.Parts parts over several A4 pages. The header row repeats at the top of each page; rows do not split across pages; the total is printed once, at the end.</p>
            <a class="ant-btn ant-btn-primary" href="/tables/print/sheet?kind=table" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Print the parts list</a>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="m-card">
        <div class="m-card-body">
            <h3 class="m-card-title">Bin labels</h3>
            <p class="m-muted">@Model.Labels labels, @Model.LabelsPerSheet to an A4 sheet (three across, seven down). Each sheet prints on its own page, with no page margin, so the labels line up with the stock.</p>
            <a class="ant-btn ant-btn-primary" href="/tables/print/sheet?kind=labels" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Print the bin labels</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
